# Life Operating System Reference

LOS_PATH=CHANGE_ME

## What Claude can do with this:
- Read $LOS_PATH/memory/projects/ to see all my projects
- Read $LOS_PATH/memory/knowledge/ for accumulated knowledge
- Read $LOS_PATH/memory/areas/ for life context (career, health, etc.)
- Append to $LOS_PATH/logs/{YYYY-MM-DD}.md to log cross-project actions
  Format: [{this-project-name}] {action}: {details}

## When to use:
- A skill or command needs context about me or my other projects
- This project relates to something tracked in LOS
- A task completes or fails and should be logged centrally

## Do NOT:
- Write to LOS memory/projects/ from another project (only append to logs/)
- Duplicate LOS knowledge into this project's context
- Read LOS files on every message — only when context is actually needed
